    "context": "{\"citation\": \"S1\", \"document_id\": \"2024-OC-207\", \"title\": \"Auto- replenishment of NETC FASTag and RuPay NCMC with UPI AutoPay\", \"circular_number\": \"207\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": \"b) Exemption from 24-Hours prior Pre-Debit Notification (PDN) for auto- replenishment of NETC FASTag and RuPay NCMC. in the Circular RBI/2024-25/64 CO.DPSS.POLC.No.S528/02-14-003/2024-25 issued by Reserve Bank of India (RBI), dated 22\\\" August 2024\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"direct_match\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S2\", \"document_id\": \"rbi:e-mandates:2026-04-21\", \"title\": \"Digital Payments – E-mandate Framework, 2026\", \"circular_number\": \"RBI/DPSS/2026-27/396\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2026-04-21\", \"text\": \"## 6. Pre-transaction Notification (a) An issuer shall send a pre-transaction notification to the customer, at least 24 hours prior to the actual charge / debit. (b) The pre-transaction notification shall, at the minimum, inform the customer about the merchant’s name, transaction amount, date / time of debit, reference number of e-mandate, reason for debit, i.e., e-mandate registered by the customer. (c) The issuer shall provider a customer with a facility to opt-out of any particular transaction or the e-mandate. Any such opt-out shall be validated by the issuer using AFA. An intimation to this effect shall be sent to the customer. (d) Pre-transaction notification is not required for e-mandates registered to auto-replenish balances of FASTag, and National Common Mobility Card (NCMC).\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"6. Pre-transaction Notification\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"direct_match\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"E-mandates\", \"UPI\", \"PPI\", \"Cards\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"operator_supplied_not_independently_verified\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 1, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": false, \"page_basis\": \"logical_markdown\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S3\", \"document_id\": \"2024-OC-207\", \"title\": \"Auto- replenishment of NETC FASTag and RuPay NCMC with UPI AutoPay\", \"circular_number\": \"207\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": \"3. All other instructions provided under the e-mandate framework shall continue to remain applicable In line with the above communications, the auto-replenishment of NETC FASTag (MCC 4784) and RuPay NCMC (MCC 7412) is permitted without 24-hrs Pre-Debited Notification under JOO1A, The Capital, B Wing, 10\\\" Floor, Bandra Kurla Complex, Bandra (E), Mumbai 400 051. T: +91 22 40009100 F: +91 22 40009101 www.npci.org.in CIN: U74990MH2008NPL189067 contact@npci.org.in\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"direct_match\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S4\", \"document_id\": \"2024-OC-207\", \"title\": \"Auto- replenishment of NETC FASTag and RuPay NCMC with UPI AutoPay\", \"circular_number\": \"207\", \"page\": 2, \"issue_date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": \"ardier wesfer aprart frre NATIONAL PAYMENTS CORPORATION OF INDIA UPI Autopay framework. Ail UP] Members shall remove the PDN validation for any UPI Autopay execution only for the mentioned MCCs. NETC FASTag and RuPay NCMC Issuer Banks to ensure that the auto-replenishment done under exception of Pre-Debit Notification as per the said guidelines shall be used only for the intended purposes of NETC FASTag and RuPay NCMC only. All UPI remitter banks, Payer PSP Banks, and concerned ecosystem stakeholders shall implement the same with immediate effect. This directive must be communicated to all relevant stakeholders for appropriate actions. Thanking You, SD/- Kunal Kalawatia Chief of Producis\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"direct_match\", \"roles\": [\"payer_psp\", \"remitter_bank\", \"issuer_bank\"], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S5\", \"document_id\": \"npci-source-ede614019fb2bb1fff724e50\", \"title\": \"Circular 78 - Reconciliation and handling declined / timed out transactions in UPI for One-time mandate block\", \"circular_number\": \"78\", \"page\": 5, \"issue_date\": null, \"text\": \"8. SMs alerts to the customer for all the mandate transaction type Member banks to send post transaction alert / notification to customers for all mandate type transactions of Create/Update/Revoke/Debit and any actions initiated after reconciliation is done. This notification to shall, at the minimum, inform about the payee details, transaction reference number, transaction amount, mandate type, date/time of debit, etc.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Annex\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"direct_match\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"inventory_unverified\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 5, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"imported_markdown\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S6\", \"document_id\": \"npci-source-82d3d77ff7e47062a2325650\", \"title\": \"Annexure-A-RBI-circular-Processing-of-emandates-on-cards-fo\", \"circular_number\": \"\", \"page\": 4, \"issue_date\": null, \"text\": \"4 for changing this mode of receiving pre-transaction notification, shall also be provided to the cardholder. 9. The pre-transaction notification shall, at the minimum, inform the cardholder about the name of the merchant, transaction amount, date / time of debit, reference number of transaction/ e-mandate, reason for debit, i.e., e-mandate registered by the cardholder. 10. On receipt of the pre-transaction notification, the cardholder shall have the facility to opt- out of that particular transaction or the e-mandate. Any such opt-out shall entail AFA validation by the issuer. On receipt of intimation of such an opt-out, the issuer shall ensure that the particular transaction is not effected / further recurring transactions are not effected (as the case may be). A confirmation intimation to this effect shall be sent to the cardholder. Post-transaction notification 11. In line with the extant instructions, the issuer shall send post-transaction alert / notification to the cardholder. This notification shall, at the minimum, inform the cardholder about the name of the merchant, transaction amount, date / time of debit, reference number of transaction / e- mandate, reason for debit, i.e., e-mandate registered by the cardholder. Transaction limit and velocity check 12. The cap / limit for e-mandate based recurring transactions without AFA will be ` 2,000/- per transaction. Transactions above this cap shall be subject to AFA\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Annex\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"direct_match\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"RuPay\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"inventory_unverified\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 5, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": false, \"origin\": \"imported_markdown\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S7\", \"document_id\": \"2024-OC-207\", \"title\": \"Auto- replenishment of NETC FASTag and RuPay NCMC with UPI AutoPay\", \"circular_number\": \"207\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": \"a) To include auto-replenishment of NETC FASTag and RuPay NCMC, as and when the balance falls below a threshold set by the customer, under the e- mandate framework.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"qualification_context\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S8\", \"document_id\": \"rbi:e-mandates:2026-04-21\", \"title\": \"Digital Payments – E-mandate Framework, 2026\", \"circular_number\": \"RBI/DPSS/2026-27/396\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2026-04-21\", \"text\": \"## 5. Processing of first transaction and subsequent recurring transactions (a) The first transaction under an e-mandate shall require AFA validation. If the first transaction is processed along with registration of the e-mandate, then AFA validation may be combined. (b) Payments under e-mandates shall not be subject to any other limits / controls set by the customer.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"5. Processing of first transaction and subsequent recurring transactions\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"qualification_context\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"E-mandates\", \"UPI\", \"PPI\", \"Cards\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"operator_supplied_not_independently_verified\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 1, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": false, \"page_basis\": \"logical_markdown\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S9\", \"document_id\": \"npci-source-ede614019fb2bb1fff724e50\", \"title\": \"Circular 78 - Reconciliation and handling declined / timed out transactions in UPI for One-time mandate block\", \"circular_number\": \"78\", \"page\": 5, \"issue_date\": null, \"text\": \"9. Maker&Checker Banks to reconcile all mandate transactions with proper maker and checker process as defined in this document. ****\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Annex\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"qualification_context\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"inventory_unverified\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 5, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"imported_markdown\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S10\", \"document_id\": \"npci-source-ede614019fb2bb1fff724e50\", \"title\": \"Circular 78 - Reconciliation and handling declined / timed out transactions in UPI for One-time mandate block\", \"circular_number\": \"78\", \"page\": 5, \"issue_date\": null, \"text\": \"NPCI NATIONALPAYMENTS CORPORATION OFINDIA\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Annex\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"qualification_context\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"inventory_unverified\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 5, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"imported_markdown\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S11\", \"document_id\": \"npci-source-82d3d77ff7e47062a2325650\", \"title\": \"Annexure-A-RBI-circular-Processing-of-emandates-on-cards-fo\", \"circular_number\": \"\", \"page\": 4, \"issue_date\": null, \"text\": \"by the cardholder. Transaction limit and velocity check 12. The cap / limit for e-mandate based recurring transactions without AFA will be ` 2,000/- per transaction. Transactions above this cap shall be subject to AFA as hitherto. 13. The limit of ` 2,000/- per transaction is applicable for all categories of merchants who accept repetitive payments based on such e-mandates. 14. Suitable velocity checks and other risk mitigation procedures shall be put in place by issuers. Withdrawal of e-mandate 15. The issuer shall provide the cardholder an online facility to withdraw any e-mandate at any point of time following which no further recurring transactions shall be allowed for the withdrawn e-mandate. (Note: The exception to this will be a pipeline transaction for which pre-transaction notification has already been sent to the cardholder, but the debit has not been communicated to or received by the cardholder, and the e-mandate withdrawal happens during the interregnum.) Information about this facility to withdraw e-mandate at any point of time, shall be clearly communicated to the cardholder at the time of registration and later on whenever felt necessary. 16. The withdrawal of any e-mandate by the cardholder shall entail AFA validation by the issuer. 17. In respect of withdrawn e-mandate/s, the acquirers shall ensure that the merchants on- boarded by them, delete all details, including\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Annex\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"qualification_context\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"RuPay\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"inventory_unverified\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 5, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": false, \"origin\": \"imported_markdown\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S12\", \"document_id\": \"npci-source-82d3d77ff7e47062a2325650\", \"title\": \"Annexure-A-RBI-circular-Processing-of-emandates-on-cards-fo\", \"circular_number\": \"\", \"page\": 3, \"issue_date\": null, \"text\": \"value of the recurring transaction; in the case of the latter, the cardholder shall clearly specify the maximum value of recurring transactions, subject to the overall cap fixed by the RBI (currently ` 2,000/- per transaction). 5. Any modification in existing e-mandate shall entail AFA validation by the issuer. Processing of first transaction and subsequent recurring transactions 6. While processing the first transaction in e-mandate based recurring transaction series, AFA validation shall be performed. If the first transaction is being performed along with the registration of e-mandate, then AFA validation may be combined. All such AFA validation shall be as per extant instructions of the RBI. 7. Subsequent recurring transactions shall be performed only for those cards which have been successfully registered and for which the first transaction was successfully authenticated and authorised. These subsequent transactions may be performed without AFA. Pre-transaction notification 8. As a risk mitigant and customer facilitation measure, the issuer shall send a pre- transaction notification to the cardholder, at least 24 hours prior to the actual charge / debit to the card. While registering e-mandate on the card, the cardholder shall be given facility to choose a mode among available options (SMS, email, etc.) for receiving the pre-transaction notification from the issuer in a clear, unambiguous manner and in an understandable language. The facility\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Annex\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"qualification_context\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"RuPay\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"inventory_unverified\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 5, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": false, \"origin\": \"imported_markdown\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S13\", \"document_id\": \"npci-source-92d050bf2cd0e823c2392797\", \"title\": \"04-Jun-2020 - Product Bulletin - Issuance of RuPay Contactless Cards & Tokenization\", \"circular_number\": \"\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": null, \"text\": \"Cards (with NCMC Offline functionality), matched off with the ongoing, fast tracked rollout of contactless acceptance for RuPay. Government of India has also stressed the need to issue such cards to every citizen as a default option for all variants i.e. Debit, Credit and Prepaid. With an emphasis on enhanced security, we urge members to on board RuPay tokenization platform to minimize exposure of sensitive data and therefore reducing risk of compromise or accidental exposure and unauthorized access to sensitive data. Below mentioned are some salient features of RuPay Tokenization: • Better security as original card details are not exposed in payment eco-system and the data is kept secured at network secure vault • New Contactless Card Issuance is not required and existing Card can be tokenized for Contactless transaction using the phone • Multiple cards can be provisioned in same application and One card can be provisioned to multiple devices/apps as per customer convenience\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"same_feature\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"RuPay\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"inventory_unverified\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": false, \"origin\": \"imported_markdown\"}}",
    "answer": "The RBI e-mandate directions exempt specified auto-replenishment mandates from pre-transaction notification, while separately requiring the issuer to send a post-transaction notification. Do not extend the pre-transaction exemption to post-transaction notices."
}
